{"n": 626, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "626.webp", "text": "NON\npO\n\n31633225\n\n33-5\n\n3321031 REPLACING DUST COVER\nRemove output shaft 33 21.000.\n/mportant!\n\nDon‘t mix up the thicker output shafts and\njoints for the BMW 325 i,\n\nPress off sealing cover (1),\n\nLoosen straps.\n\nRemove circlip (2).\nPress off cap (3) and dust cover,\n\nPress output shaft out of constant velocity\njoint.\n\nImportant!\n\nBall hub must rest on counterpressure\nplate (P).\n\nDo not disassemble joint if not absolutely\n\nnecessary.\nCheck joint for dirt or damage.\n\nIf the joint has to be disassembled (dirty),\nfirst electrically inscribe position of ball hub,\nball cage and joint to each other on face.\nAbsolute cleanliness is important during\nassembly work.\n\n3033075\n\n3033076\n\n3023051\n\nPull wheel end dust cover off and on over the\noutput shaft,\n\nSlide transmission end dust cover over splined\nshaft,\n\nImportant!\n\nBe careful not to damage new dust covers,\nProtect it from the sharp edges on the splined\nshaft with a suitable sleeve,\n\nUse repair kit,\n\nClean splines of joint to remove grease.\nCoat splines with Loctite No, 270.\nCaution!\n\nKeep Loctite out of bal! surfaces.\n\nPress on joint and cap (3), while holding the\noutput shaft with Special Tool 33 2 100.\nInstall circlip.\n\nPack joint and dust cover with grease*.\nClean sealing surfaces for dust cover to remove.\n\ngrease.\nCoat large diameter end of dust cover with an\n\nadhesive* and mount with new clamps.\nSeal and install sealing cover with Curil.\n\n* See Specifications 3", "words": [["NON", 0.1651, 0.7062, 0.1839, 0.7129], ["pO", 0.1581, 0.7135, 0.2021, 0.7215], ["31633225", 0.1905, 0.7414, 0.2447, 0.7493], ["33-5", 0.4732, 0.0325, 0.5431, 0.0637], ["3321031", 0.2639, 0.0703, 0.3121, 0.0822], ["REPLACING", 0.3267, 0.0703, 0.3901, 0.0822], ["DUST", 0.3936, 0.071, 0.4225, 0.0822], ["COVER", 0.426, 0.0703, 0.4645, 0.0822], ["Remove", 0.2644, 0.1034, 0.3029, 0.1147], ["output", 0.306, 0.1048, 0.3